# Does identifying one item of a flavoured kind teach the KIND? This is the
# oracle for inc-bj4z.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/amulet-idtype.keys 1
#
# Take an unidentified Periapt of Wisdom (an amulet) and an unidentified ring,
# identify the pack, then take one more of each and read the name the game
# gives it. The ring is the control: its type was in Item::MakeKnown's
# hand-written list and it always learned. The amulet's type was not in that
# list, so before the fix it never learned and every amulet of the same kind
# had to be identified again.
#
# WHY THE MEASUREMENT IS THE In-the-Air LINE. "Acquire Unknown Item" is wizard
# menu case 5 (src/Debug.cpp:659), which calls SetKnown(0), so what arrives is
# unidentified and lands in the Inventory Manager's In-the-Air slot. That one
# line therefore reads either the flavour ("? pearl amulet") or the true name
# ("? Periapt of Wisdom"), and nothing else on the screen can be mistaken for
# it. The leading '?' is the unknown blessed/cursed marker and stays either
# way; it is not part of what this measures.
#
# WHY BOTH AMULETS ARE THE SAME KIND. A flavour belongs to an EFFECT, not to
# an item (Game::SetFlavors, src/Item.cpp:310), so two amulets that read the
# same flavour are two amulets of the same kind. Both here read "pearl
# amulet".
#
# [w] asks "Enter wizard mode?" the FIRST time only; after that it opens the
# wizard menu directly, so a second [y] would pick the menu's y) entry --
# which is Create Trap, and the run then dies at "Enter Trap Name:".
# [s] stows the in-air item in the backpack (src/Managers.cpp:835). The
# manager will not close while anything is still in the air.
#
# The RIGHT counts are indices into ItemGlyphs (src/Tables.cpp:320), counted
# from zero: ring 26, amulet 27. A miscount lands on another category and the
# following @until then fails loudly rather than measuring the wrong item.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

w
y
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*27
@until "Periapt of Wisdom" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:amulet-1-in-air
s
ENTER

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*26
@until "Fire Resistance" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:ring-1-in-air
s
ENTER

w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*27
@until "Periapt of Wisdom" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:amulet-2-in-air
s
ENTER

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*26
@until "Fire Resistance" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:ring-2-in-air
s
ENTER

@quit
